-- 167 — AUTUMN LEAVES (CHILL). Jazz standard, 74 BPM, 4/4, one cycle = one bar.
-- Every ingredient is pulled from ~/tunepile; nothing here is invented:
--
-- CHANGES — chords/progressions.txt, two corpus families taken verbatim (6-note stacks):
--   ii-V-I-jazz [g] = Am7  -> D7   -> Gmaj7  -> Gmaj7
--   ii-V-I-jazz [c] = Dm7  -> G7   -> Cmaj7  -> Cmaj7
-- Together they ARE the tune's cycle: ii-V-I in G, then ii-V-I in C, eight bars.
--   found via: tools/search.sh --source chords 'ii-V-I-jazz' 'key:g' --body
-- The corpus's minor families (minor-ii-V-i) did NOT yield the half-diminished chord
-- this tune usually carries, so I used the two major families instead of faking one.
--
-- MELODY — the head's opening, from the tab corpus:
--   tabs-tidal/Cassidy_Eva_-_Autumn_Leaves.gp4-d5c9a4e5.tidal
--   header: 120 bpm | 2/4 | key CMajor | 41 bars
-- That file writes 32 beats per cycle (16 bars of 2/4), so I re-barred its first phrase
-- onto this grid (one cycle = one 4/4 bar) and thinned it to single notes: the DESCENT
-- (a4 e5 d5 c5) and its ANSWER (b4 d4 g4 d4, then b4 a3 c5 b3 d5 e5) are the tune's
-- pitches and order; the rhythm is mine. The tab spells flats sharp-wise (ds = Eb).
--
-- DRUMS — feel and accent velocities from the Magenta jazz performance:
--   midi/groove/groove/drummer1/session1/48_jazz_93_beat_4-4.mid  (93 BPM, style jazz)
--   via tools/midi_to_tidal.py --drums: feathered kick gains 0.13 / 0.30, snare accents
--   0.39 / 0.58, ride accents 0.87 / 0.84. The swing pattern is mine; the corpus fixed
--   the dynamic shape, which is exactly the information a hand-written groove lacks.
--
-- Raw kit: the SOFT banks were chosen by inspecting the corpus listings, not by guessing:
--   h2ogmbd:3 = Kick-Soft.wav, h2ogmsn:8 = Snare-Soft.wav, h2ogmcy:18 = Ride-Soft.wav.
-- Orbit map: 0 drums (dry; orbit 0 is the master's sidechain detector) | 1 bass dry |
-- 2 chords into the dub delay | 3 melody into reverb | 4 texture through tape |
-- 5 send accents with a silent reset clock. Every pitched lane carries keyShift 0.
-- @scene {"title":"Autumn Leaves (chill)","cps":0.30833333333333335,"quantize":4}

-- ORBIT 0: the kit, dry. Feathered kick (corpus gains) and a soft snare on 2 and 4.
d1 $ s "h2ogmbd:3 ~ ~ ~ h2ogmbd:3 ~ ~ ~" # orbit 0 # gain "0.13 ~ ~ ~ 0.30 ~ ~ ~" # speed 0.95 # hpf 40 # lpf 2600 # release 0.10 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0 # room 0

d2 $ s "~ ~ ~ ~ h2ogmsn:8 ~ ~ ~" # orbit 0 # gain 0.39 # speed 0.9 # nudge 0.012 # hpf 220 # lpf 4800 # release 0.12 # verbSend 0.05 # room 0.25 # verbT60 0.8 # ddSend 0

-- Swung ride from the jazz performance's accent shape (0.87 on the downbeat, 0.84 later).
d3 $ swingBy 0.16 8 $ s "h2ogmcy:18 ~ h2ogmcy:18 h2ogmcy:18 h2ogmcy:18 ~ h2ogmcy:18 h2ogmcy:18" # orbit 0 # gain "0.42 ~ 0.28 0.22 0.40 ~ 0.28 0.22" # hpf 300 # lpf 9000 # release 0.16 # verbSend 0.04 # room 0.2 # verbT60 0.8 # ddSend 0

-- ORBIT 1: bass, dry. Roots of the eight-bar corpus cycle, two per bar.
d6 $ struct "t ~ ~ ~ t ~ ~ ~" $ slow 8 $ n "<a1 d2 g1 g1 d2 g1 c2 c2>" # s "dubsynth" # orbit 1 # gain 0.5 # amp 0.7 # waveMix 0.16 # subMix 0.4 # subTone 0.28 # detune 0.05 # cutoff 500 # fenv 1.8 # res 0.2 # drive 0.12 # attack 0.008 # sustain 0.4 # release 0.25 # hpf 34 # lpf 800 # keyShift 0 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

-- ORBIT 2: the changes, one corpus voicing per bar, into the dotted-8th dub delay.
d4 $ cat [note "a3 a4 c5 e5 g5 b5", note "d3 d4 fs4 a4 c5 e5", note "g3 g4 b4 d5 fs5 a5", note "g3 g4 b4 d5 fs5 a5", note "d3 d4 f4 a4 c5 e5", note "g3 g4 b4 d5 f5 a5", note "c3 c4 e4 g4 b4 d5", note "c3 c4 e4 g4 b4 d5"] # s "hoRhodes" # orbit 2 # gain 0.62 # amp 0.34 # cutoff 3400 # waveMix 0.09 # sustain 1.2 # release 1.6 # pan 0.46 # keyShift 0 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0.28 # ddSend 0.28 # ddHp 900 # ddLp 4200 # ddDrive 0.06 # ddWow 0.05 # ddCross 0.6 # ddDuck 0.5 # verbSend 0.10 # room 0.35 # verbT60 1.6

-- ORBIT 3: the head, into a long reverb. Four-bar phrase (two cycles), then it repeats.
d5 $ slow 2 $ note "<[a4 ~ ~ e5 ~ d5 ~ c5] [~ b4 ~ d4 ~ g4 ~ d4] [b4 ~ a3 ~ c5 ~ b3 ~] [~ d5 ~ e5 ~ e4 ~ g4]>" # s "hoRhodes" # orbit 3 # gain 0.66 # amp 0.4 # cutoff 4200 # attack 0.01 # release 0.5 # pan 0.6 # keyShift 0 # vib 0.10 # vibRate 5.0 # verbSend 0.30 # room 0.65 # verbT60 2.6 # ddSend 0 # delayfeedback 0

-- ORBIT 4: texture through tape — the padded comping behind the head, quarter-note dyads.
d7 $ struct "t ~ ~ ~ t ~ ~ ~" $ slow 4 $ note "<[e4,g4,b4] [d4,f4,a4] [b3,d4,g4] [c4,e4,g4]>" # s "sweetChords" # orbit 4 # gain 0.34 # amp 0.4 # cutoff 3600 # fmIndex 1.1 # ratio 1.5 # drive 1.0 # sub 0.35 # width 0.7 # attack 0.25 # release 2.0 # sustain 1.4 # pan 0.52 # keyShift 0 # tape 0.22 # tapeWow 0.16 # tapeHiss 0.008 # verbSend 0.18 # room 0.45 # verbT60 2.2 # ddSend 0

-- ORBIT 5: one brush-sweep accent at the end of the eight-bar cycle, with its reset clock.
-- Accent on the LAST bar of the eight-bar cycle: whenmod 8 7 = cycles where c mod 8 >= 7.
-- (whenT with a hand-rolled `mod` on the cycle number does not typecheck: cycles are Rational.)
d8 $ whenmod 8 7 (stutWith 2 0.0625 (|* gain 0.55)) $ s "~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ h2ogmsn:13 ~" # orbit 5 # gain 0.22 # speed 0.9 # hpf 400 # lpf 5200 # sustain 0.5 # release 0.6 # ddSend 0.30 # delayfeedback 0.30 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # ddHp 900 # ddLp 4400 # ddDrive 0.08 # ddWow 0.05 # ddCross 0.6 # ddDuck 0.5 # verbSend 0.25 # room 0.5 # verbT60 1.8

d9 $ s "h2ogmhh:13*8" # orbit 5 # gain 0 # begin 0 # end 0.01 # sustain 0.001 # ddSend 0 # delayfeedback 0 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # ddHp 900 # ddLp 4400 # ddDrive 0.08 # ddWow 0.05 # ddCross 0.6 # ddDuck 0.5 # verbSend 0 # room 0
